es: glucose is normal for presentation despite diabetes history", "Infectious etiology (e.g., sepsis): no localized infection signs, but high WBC could represent reactive leukocytosis — less likely given blasts", "Neoplastic visceral mass syndrome: weight loss and systemic features suggest malignancy but lack localized symptoms"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional symptoms (weight loss, night sweats, fever)", "Severe leukocytosis with blasts (57,500/mm³)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.11193629075055544, "danger": 0.95, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Visual and gait changes are more consistent with myeloid processes (e.g., cord compression from AML) than lymphoproliferative disease."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.3861821525197672, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Diabetes and normal glucose do not exclude lymphoid blast processes, but provide minor disconfirmation."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.85, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute lymphoblastic leuke